.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-authorize - Authorize a payment (prepare, sign, and broadcast)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments authorize  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prepare the transaction that calls authorize() on the RAIL0 contract,
pulling funds from the payer into escrow.

.PP
The payer must have created and signed the payment first via
\&'payments create -p' (create + sign in one atomic step).
The API returns 202 immediately. The payment stays at "signed" until
rail0-indexer confirms the on-chain event and the API transitions it to
"authorized". Poll 'payments get \&' until payment=authorized
and the authorize transaction shows confirmed.

.PP
Pass --private-key (-p): the CLI signs locally and broadcasts in one step.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for authorize

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Caller's secp256k1 private key (0x-prefixed hex); signs and broadcasts in one step

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	Max time to wait when --wait is set

.PP
\fB-w\fP, \fB--wait\fP[=false]
	Block until the operation confirms on-chain (or fails)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # 1. Payer creates and signs the payment in one step
  rail0 payments create --from 0xBuyer… --to 0xMerchant… \\
    --token 0x3600… --amount 1.00 --chain-id 5042002 -p 0xPayerKey…

  # 2. Payee authorizes
  rail0 payments authorize <rail0Id> -p 0xPayeeKey…
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
